[12.355261, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Docker Api Miner campaign\r\n========================================================\r\n\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: docker-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.102\r\n\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\n   T1133      External Remote Services                   [persistence]  step 1: exposed Docker API (external service)\r\n   T1610      Deploy Container                           [execution]  step 2: deploy privileged container\r\n   T1611      Escape to Host                             [privilege-escalation]  step 3: container escape to host\r\n   T1496      Resource Hijacking                         [impact]  step 4: cryptomining\r\n   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 5: cron persistence\r\n   T1543.002  Systemd Service                            [persistence]  step 6: systemd persistence\r\n\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\n   ip     198.51.100.102\r\n   c2     update-docker[.]example[.]cn\r\n   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]docker[.]evil[:]3333\r\n   wallet 4A0000000000000000009e202e3a533f\r\n\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n"]
[12.355349, "o", "MITRE ATT&CK(R): (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0 (attack.mitre.org).\r\nCVE/CVSS: U.S. National Vulnerability Database, nvd.nist.gov (public-domain U.S.-Gov work).\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@a74f6f119aac:/app# "]
