[156.32583, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Report — Docker API Miner Campaign\n\n## Overview\nThis report analyzes software vulnerability involvement in the initial entry of the attacker into `docker-prod-01`.\n\n## Assessment of Vulnerability-Driven Entry\n- **Vulnerability Feed Analysis**: The host vulnerability scan database `/sas/vulns.json` contains zero reported software CVE entries (`/sas/vulns.json`).\n- **Rebuttal of CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)**: Draft change ticket CHG-1943 row 2 incorrectly proposed patching CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep RDP) (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`). Forensics confirms the host is running Ubuntu 22.04 LTS Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release`). CVE-2019-0708 is a Windows Remote Desktop Services RDP vulnerability and is completely inapplicable to this Linux infrastructure.\n- **Web Scanning/Probing Analysis**: Nginx web server logs record automated probing from attacker IP `198.51.100.102` including webshell upload attempts (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:1`), Log4Shell OOB LDAP lookup attempts returning HTTP 500 (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:2`), and Struts2 OGNL probes (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:3`). Forensic analysis indicates these were general reconnaissance probes and not the primary vector used to gain root-level host access.\n- **Actual Vector**: Primary entry was gained directly by abusing the unauthenticated Docker Engine API exposed on port 2375 (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`, `/sas/baseline.json:1`). This constitutes exposure of an unauthenticated management service (MITRE ATT&CK T1133) rather than a software vulnerability exploit.\n\n## Confidence Statement\n- **Confidence**: HIGH\n- **Rationale**: No host software CVEs were exploited (`/sas/vulns.json`). Forensic artifacts under `/disk` (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`, `/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:1`) conclusively prove direct exploitation of the unauthenticated Docker TCP socket.\nEOF\n"]
[156.32655, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md"]
[156.326577, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # Vulnerability Report — Docker API Miner Campaign\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
