[163.901304, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline & Configuration Weakness Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nA review of baseline checks and forensic configuration files on `docker-prod-01` identified critical misconfigurations that enabled the initial compromise and host escape.\n\n## Detailed Configuration Findings\n\n### 1. Unauthenticated Docker Engine API Exposed on Public Interface (CHK-05 / BAS-01)\n- **Check ID**: CHK-05\n- **Capability**: BAS-01\n- **Finding Path**: `/etc/docker/daemon.json` (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`, `/sas/baseline.json:1`)\n- **Weakness**: The Docker daemon configuration enabled TCP listener binding on `0.0.0.0:2375` without TLS authentication or IP restricted access control (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`).\n- **Impact**: Allowed remote unauthenticated users, such as attacker IP `198.51.100.102` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:1`), full root-equivalent control over the Docker Engine daemon.\n\n### 2. Unrestricted Privileged Container Execution & Host Mounts\n- **Finding Path**: `/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh` (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:1`)\n- **Weakness**: The host lacked Docker daemon runtime security options (e.g., AppArmor/Seccomp profiles, disabling `--privileged`, restricting host path bind mounts).\n- **Impact**: Allowed the attacker to spawn a privileged container mounting the host's root filesystem (`/`) and escape to host context.\n\n### 3. Lack of Service Integrity Monitoring & Silent Persistence Exposure\n- **Finding Path**: `/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1`)\n- **Weakness**: System integrity monitoring failed to flag unauthorized creation of systemd unit files in `/etc/systemd/system/` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1`), leaving persistence hidden from SOC EDR alerts (`/sas/alerts.json`).\n\n### 4. Absence of Network Ingress Firewall Restrictions\n- **Finding Path**: `/var/log/nginx/access.log` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:1`)\n- **Weakness**: System-level firewall (iptables/ufw) or cloud security groups permitted arbitrary external connections from internet addresses (`198.51.100.102`) to administrative management ports.\n\n## Recommendations Summary\n1. Restrict Docker API socket to local UNIX socket `/var/run/docker.sock` or enforce Mutual TLS (mTLS) with firewall ingress controls (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`).\n2. Implement container security policies prohibiting `--privileged` mode and root host filesystem mounts (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:1`).\n3. Expand EDR file integrity monitoring (FIM) to audit systemd unit directories (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1`).\nEOF\n"]
[163.902766, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md"]
